    rationale:
      "The agent found a real dead-click bug in the leads dashboard (src/app/dashboard/leads/leads-client.tsx) affecting both due-queue summary panels that surface a commerce-catalog gap: 'Commerce catalogs missing' (Add catalog button) and 'Commerce catalogs unsynced' (Edit catalog button). Both call openCommerceEditor(lead), which only sets commerceEditSlug/commerceDraftItems state — no scroll, no filter change. commerceCatalogsMissing/commerceCatalogsUnsynced are computed from the full unfiltered `leads` array (so a lead in any pipeline stage can appear there), but the actual inline catalog-editor panel only mounts inside the main table's `filteredLeads.map(...)` loop, and filteredLeads excludes any lead that doesn't match the operator's current stage filter or search query. Concrete failure scenario: operator clicks a stage filter (e.g. 'Discovered') or types a search term that excludes a lead sitting in the missing/unsynced queue (e.g. a lead in `paid` stage); that lead's table row never mounts; clicking 'Add catalog'/'Edit catalog' in the still-visible summary panel updates commerceEditSlug internally but the editor panel renders nowhere on the page — no scroll, no error, no visible feedback of any kind, for keyboard, screen-reader, and sighted users alike, until the operator happens to reset the filter/search and locate the row themselves. The sibling openNotesEditor already has the equivalent fix for its own 'soft prompt from Work next / follow-up queue' call sites (bring the row into view via requestAnimationFrame + scrollIntoView on `lead-notes-${slug}` when a `reason` is passed) — that precedent was simply never applied to openCommerceEditor's two due-queue call sites when they were added. Verified this is genuinely scoped to those two call sites: grepped every openCommerceEditor call site (3 total) — the third, inside the main table's own per-row 'Add/Edit catalog' toggle button, only ever fires on an already-rendered (hence already-filter-matching) row, so it needs no change. Also confirmed openNotesEditor's own reason-triggered call sites (after Send follow-up / the initial discovery-call auto-open) are exempt from this bug class for the same reason — both fire on a lead the operator just acted on via a button inside the already-visible table row itself, never from a queue-only summary panel outside it; only the commerce editor is invoked directly from a due-queue panel that draws from the unfiltered lead set.\n\nFixed by giving openCommerceEditor an optional `opts?: { bringIntoView?: boolean }` parameter: when passed, it resets `filterStage` to `\"all\"` and `searchQuery` to `\"\"` (guaranteeing the target lead is in filteredLeads) and schedules the same requestAnimationFrame + scrollIntoView-on-`lead-commerce-${slug}` pattern openNotesEditor already uses. Passed `{ bringIntoView: true }` from both due-queue panel call sites; left the in-row toggle call site unchanged (default no-op, so an operator's intentional filter/search selection is never reset by clicking Add/Edit catalog on a row already in view). This is the kind of bug AGENT_PROTOCOL itself flags as untestable by the existing Vitest suite (no @testing-library/react harness in this repo), so verification was done directly against a running dev server rather than a new unit test: seeded local.db with a demo lead (example-bakery) set to stage=paid plus a commerceAddon order (so it qualifies for 'Commerce catalogs missing'), used Playwright (a globally-installed browser, not a project dependency) to apply a stage filter that excludes that lead from the table, clicked 'Add catalog' in the still-visible summary panel, and confirmed `#lead-commerce-example-bakery` — absent from the DOM before the click — mounts and is visible immediately after, with the filter having reset. Also verified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors), npm run lint (clean), npx vitest run (2842 passed, unchanged — no test surface exists for this class of bug per the above), and a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same 42-route ○/ƒ split); dev server killed, port 3000 confirmed freed, local.db deleted afterward. NEXT_STEPS unchanged — all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked; this is a dashboard-UX correctness fix on an already-shipped feature, not a resolution of any gated item. Diff-gate anchor moves to 5534394 (this iteration's own starting tip).",
